(1279111, 162981, 12448, '<td valign="top">Oh, the poor baby!  All chained up :(  And he looks pretty ticked off!  It''s a great candid shot but doesn''t come off with the portrait flair.  The light and overall composition works well with this shot but the conditions surrounding dog do influence how I feel about the shot. The shap metal roof, the short, short chain make me feel sorry for the puppy.  If this was just about any other challenge besides a portrait challenge this would score higher but as is, a 5</td>', 'Oh, the poor baby!  All chained up :(  And he looks pretty ticked off!  It''s a great candid shot but doesn''t come off with the portrait flair.  The light and overall composition works well with this shot but the conditions surrounding dog do influence how I feel about the shot. The shap metal roof, the short, short chain make me feel sorry for the puppy.  If this was just about any other challenge besides a portrait challenge this would score higher but as is, a 5', '2005-04-08 11:33:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(1279112, 162909, 32378, '<td valign="top">I like the depth of field and composition.  Cat''s face seems a little dark maybe lightening just a touch would have helped.</td>', 'I like the depth of field and composition.  Cat''s face seems a little dark maybe lightening just a touch would have helped.', '2005-04-08 11:34:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(1279116, 162569, 32378, '<td valign="top">I would have liked a litle more depth of field.  Overall a nice picture although something show more of the cat''s character would have helped.</td>', 'I would have liked a litle more depth of field.  Overall a nice picture although something show more of the cat''s character would have helped.', '2005-04-08 11:35:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(1279126, 162985, 12448, '<td valign="top">Ah, a classic pose, almost Egyptian in it''s nature.  But the light is so harsh and bright and the shadows just hurt this on so many levels.  I really like the idea and the set up, but maybe a diffused light and a darker background, possibly even black with the light might work better, would help absorb some of the light and hide the shadow.  As is a 5</td>', 'Ah, a classic pose, almost Egyptian in it''s nature.  But the light is so harsh and bright and the shadows just hurt this on so many levels.  I really like the idea and the set up, but maybe a diffused light and a darker background, possibly even black with the light might work better, would help absorb some of the light and hide the shadow.  As is a 5', '2005-04-08 11:41:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(1279129, 162550, 12448, '<td valign="top">Oh dear, someone had a LOT of fun didn''t they?  LOL!  This is a classic candid shot of a dog at the beach and I love it for that.  But for a portrait challene, it falls just a bit short.  Maybe a slightly tighter crop on the left and top to really bring the dog main focus of the shot, leaving the beach and water as your negative space filler.  The light is a bit bright but then again, how you gonna difuse the sun? :)  I had this at a 5 but am going to bump up to a 6</td>', 'Oh dear, someone had a LOT of fun didn''t they?  LOL!  This is a classic candid shot of a dog at the beach and I love it for that.  But for a portrait challene, it falls just a bit short.  Maybe a slightly tighter crop on the left and top to really bring the dog main focus of the shot, leaving the beach and water as your negative space filler.  The light is a bit bright but then again, how you gonna difuse the sun? :)  I had this at a 5 but am going to bump up to a 6', '2005-04-08 11:43:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(1279131, 163050, 32378, '<td valign="top">I''m bumping this up.  I would have liked a little more detail on the left of the dog.</td>', 'I''m bumping this up.  I would have liked a little more detail on the left of the dog.', '2005-04-08 11:44:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(1279137, 161985, 32378, '<td valign="top">Wonder if a tighter crop or portrait crop would have helped.  I like the angle of the dog''s head,  tends to show some of hish character.</td>', 'Wonder if a tighter crop or portrait crop would have helped.  I like the angle of the dog''s head,  tends to show some of hish character.', '2005-04-08 11:45:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(1279138, 161863, 32378, '<td valign="top">Not a bad picture.  Somehow the dog''s expresion doesn''t match the fun loving look I would have suspected from the frisbee.</td>', 'Not a bad picture.  Somehow the dog''s expresion doesn''t match the fun loving look I would have suspected from the frisbee.', '2005-04-08 11:46:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(1279139, 162812, 32378, '<td valign="top">I think this picure would have been better if the dog had not been so close to the fence so that the detail of the fence could have been blurred.</td>', 'I think this picure would have been better if the dog had not been so close to the fence so that the detail of the fence could have been blurred.', '2005-04-08 11:47:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(1279141, 161741, 12448, '<td valign="top">Oooooo, pretty black kitty!  And you caught details!  Good for you!  That is the hardest thing to do, getting any kind of detail on a black animal.  The light is a bit harsh though, need to diffuse that darn sun sometimes, LOL!  The bottom is a real hot spot, this being an advance challenge, you could seperate that area and diffuse it just a bit so it''s not fighting for my attention.  <br/> <br/>I love the eyes, very intent and it''s not the sun that''s making them look that intense, something has caught his/her eye!  It''s hard to tell if they are standing or sitting and while that might not seem a big deal, if you look to the right of the shot, the back end can be a bit of a distraction.    Maybe a tighter crop on the right, taking the cat slightly off center, looser on the left if you have room so his/her eyes are leading you out of the shot.  And then working that upper right area to make the back end darken so it''s not a distraction.<br/> <br/>I started this at a 5 but am bumping to a 6, if you work on this I would love to see the new picture.</td>', 'Oooooo, pretty black kitty!  And you caught details!  Good for you!  That is the hardest thing to do, getting any kind of detail on a black animal.  The light is a bit harsh though, need to diffuse that darn sun sometimes, LOL!  The bottom is a real hot spot, this being an advance challenge, you could seperate that area and diffuse it just a bit so it''s not fighting for my attention.   I love the eyes, very intent and it''s not the sun that''s making them look that intense, something has caught his/her eye!  It''s hard to tell if they are standing or sitting and while that might not seem a big deal, if you look to the right of the shot, the back end can be a bit of a distraction.    Maybe a tighter crop on the right, taking the cat slightly off center, looser on the left if you have room so his/her eyes are leading you out of the shot.  And then working that upper right area to make the back end darken so it''s not a distraction. I started this at a 5 but am bumping to a 6, if you work on this I would love to see the new picture.', '2005-04-08 11:48:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(1279143, 163086, 32378, '<td valign="top">I like the character shown here, like the cat doesn ''t know what to make of the reflection.  I think a little lighter colorin the back ground would have made the cat stand out more.</td>', 'I like the character shown here, like the cat doesn ''t know what to make of the reflection.  I think a little lighter colorin the back ground would have made the cat stand out more.', '2005-04-08 11:50:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(1279144, 162541, 32378, '<td valign="top">I think all the yellow in the back ground makes this look a litte over exposed or something or maybe the edges are over sharpened.</td>', 'I think all the yellow in the back ground makes this look a litte over exposed or something or maybe the edges are over sharpened.', '2005-04-08 11:51:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(1279147, 161481, 32378, '<td valign="top">Nice shot. going to bump it up.</td>', 'Nice shot. going to bump it up.', '2005-04-08 11:52:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(1279151, 162960, 12448, '<td valign="top">Awwwwwww!  How cool!  I had my cat at my wedding, she was an honorary flower cat :)<br/> <br/>This is a great shot, the black and white works very well but it seems overly smooth, not sure if that''s neat image or what.  And since this is supposed to be Pet portrait, I would really like to see more focus on the dog himself/herself.  The couple is very nice I''m sure and this a great reminder for the wedding album but were any taken of just the dog? :)  Giving it a 6 for a couple of reasons, the biggest being that people are in it and competing for attention with the dog.</td>', 'Awwwwwww!  How cool!  I had my cat at my wedding, she was an honorary flower cat :) This is a great shot, the black and white works very well but it seems overly smooth, not sure if that''s neat image or what.  And since this is supposed to be Pet portrait, I would really like to see more focus on the dog himself/herself.  The couple is very nice I''m sure and this a great reminder for the wedding album but were any taken of just the dog? :)  Giving it a 6 for a couple of reasons, the biggest being that people are in it and competing for attention with the dog.', '2005-04-08 11:52:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(1279155, 161679, 32378, '<td valign="top">I would have liked to see more of the dog.</td>', 'I would have liked to see more of the dog.', '2005-04-08 11:53:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(1279159, 162850, 32378, '<td valign="top">The eyes are beautiful.  Your exposure is also very nice.  However, I would have liked to see more of its face.</td>', 'The eyes are beautiful.  Your exposure is also very nice.  However, I would have liked to see more of its face.', '2005-04-08 11:54:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(1279160, 162781, 12448, '<td valign="top">Nope, he sure doesn''t!  AND you don''t have to feed him, walk him, brush him, play with him, he''s cute but darn so boring! :)<br/> <br/>Nice shot but the background is very distracting and the highlight on the right is also very distracting.  A little more depth of color on the dog, really bringing out the brown would make this a very cute shot overall.  A 5</td>', 'Nope, he sure doesn''t!  AND you don''t have to feed him, walk him, brush him, play with him, he''s cute but darn so boring! :) Nice shot but the background is very distracting and the highlight on the right is also very distracting.  A little more depth of color on the dog, really bringing out the brown would make this a very cute shot overall.  A 5', '2005-04-08 11:55:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(1279164, 162819, 12448, '<td valign="top">What a lucky shot!  Talk about timing! :)<br/> <br/>This is a fun shot but not really a portrait.  The dog is clearly having a lot of fun and very intent on grabbing that stick!  The lighting on the left makes me say, "Oh yeah, beautiful!" it loses all it''s appeal by the time I get to the right of the shot. Overblow and jpeg factors are really evident on that side.  A 5</td>', 'What a lucky shot!  Talk about timing! :) This is a fun shot but not really a portrait.  The dog is clearly having a lot of fun and very intent on grabbing that stick!  The lighting on the left makes me say, "Oh yeah, beautiful!" it loses all it''s appeal by the time I get to the right of the shot. Overblow and jpeg factors are really evident on that side.  A 5', '2005-04-08 11:57:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(1279167, 160815, 12448, '<td valign="top">Nope, not a problem at all, love the expression.  This is a very cute shot  but not really in the portrait area as far as style.  I used my magic envelopes and if you even cropped so you just had the head area it would fit much better as far as meeting the challenge.  The light is a bit harsh but hey, what can do about the sun? ;)  A 5</td>', 'Nope, not a problem at all, love the expression.  This is a very cute shot  but not really in the portrait area as far as style.  I used my magic envelopes and if you even cropped so you just had the head area it would fit much better as far as meeting the challenge.  The light is a bit harsh but hey, what can do about the sun? ;)  A 5', '2005-04-08 11:58:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(1279187, 161749, 12448, '<td valign="top">How adorable!  I love calico kitties and this one is no exception though I would like to see more of it! :)  Cute idea, nice candid but the tree in the middle is very distracting, maybe if you cropped more on the  right, making the tree the right edge, taking the kitty just off center but with my magic envelopes, it looks very nice.  Had at a 5 but am going to bump to a 6 for cuteness and nice capture!</td>', 'How adorable!  I love calico kitties and this one is no exception though I would like to see more of it! :)  Cute idea, nice candid but the tree in the middle is very distracting, maybe if you cropped more on the  right, making the tree the right edge, taking the kitty just off center but with my magic envelopes, it looks very nice.  Had at a 5 but am going to bump to a 6 for cuteness and nice capture!', '2005-04-08 12:09:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(1279225, 163082, 6519, '<td valign="top">A portrait with a difference, and I like it. Normally wrinkled or creased backgrounds can be such a no-no, but the folds of the blanket in the foreground actually add to the cozy at-ease feeling of the cat''s posture. Good focus exactly where it needs to be. 8</td>', 'A portrait with a difference, and I like it. Normally wrinkled or creased backgrounds can be such a no-no, but the folds of the blanket in the foreground actually add to the cozy at-ease feeling of the cat''s posture. Good focus exactly where it needs to be. 8', '2005-04-08 12:25:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(1279233, 161983, 12448, '<td valign="top">Ohhhhhhh, so cute!  Love puppies and that fat little belly just begging to be scratched and rubbed!  Thisis a wonderful overall shot with just a few issues to me.  One is the carpet, the pattern is very nice but for this shot, ends up being very distracting.  I like the dark in the upper part and I''m guessing natural light from a window?  Very nice again but a few hot spots on the dog, mostly the feet and upper back.  Had at a 5 but going to bump to a 6</td>', 'Ohhhhhhh, so cute!  Love puppies and that fat little belly just begging to be scratched and rubbed!  Thisis a wonderful overall shot with just a few issues to me.  One is the carpet, the pattern is very nice but for this shot, ends up being very distracting.  I like the dark in the upper part and I''m guessing natural light from a window?  Very nice again but a few hot spots on the dog, mostly the feet and upper back.  Had at a 5 but going to bump to a 6', '2005-04-08 12:28:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(1279247, 161827, 12448, '<td valign="top">Aw, cute!  Love the big eyes but it looks like you might have used a filler flash?  Great detail but the light is a bit harsh on the cat''s eyes and the white part and his whiskers on the left disappear into the background.  The border is just a bit heavy for my taste.  Maybe if you could seperate the cat from the back and work with them on different layers so they dont'' blend so much on the right?  Had at a 5 but bumping to a 6</td>', 'Aw, cute!  Love the big eyes but it looks like you might have used a filler flash?  Great detail but the light is a bit harsh on the cat''s eyes and the white part and his whiskers on the left disappear into the background.  The border is just a bit heavy for my taste.  Maybe if you could seperate the cat from the back and work with them on different layers so they dont'' blend so much on the right?  Had at a 5 but bumping to a 6', '2005-04-08 12:37:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(1279287, 161470, 31443, '<td valign="top">Naughty puddytat! Get him a scratchpost ;) like the way his eyes came out so deep and mysterious....</td>', 'Naughty puddytat! Get him a scratchpost ;) like the way his eyes came out so deep and mysterious....', '2005-04-08 12:55:53.000000', NULL, 1),
