(1281581, 162950, 12448, '<td valign="top">Clyde is one cool cat, no doubt!  I love the pose, the backgroun with the exception of the jeans in teh back on the right?  Look like someone was sitting there?  Also the flash is a bit much, maybe different lighting?  A 6</td>', 'Clyde is one cool cat, no doubt!  I love the pose, the backgroun with the exception of the jeans in teh back on the right?  Look like someone was sitting there?  Also the flash is a bit much, maybe different lighting?  A 6', '2005-04-10 00:54:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(1281582, 162678, 12448, '<td valign="top">You are so mean!  The poor dear! :)<br/> <br/>This is a cute shot but overdone with the props.  The stuffed dog, the bandana, the back drop are all competing with a very adorable bunny rabbit!  Get a plain background, black would be wonderful with this little one and get rid of all the other stuff.  The lighting looks decent, I''m thinking it might be from a window?  If so, great!  A 6</td>', 'You are so mean!  The poor dear! :) This is a cute shot but overdone with the props.  The stuffed dog, the bandana, the back drop are all competing with a very adorable bunny rabbit!  Get a plain background, black would be wonderful with this little one and get rid of all the other stuff.  The lighting looks decent, I''m thinking it might be from a window?  If so, great!  A 6', '2005-04-10 00:56:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(1281583, 163052, 12448, '<td valign="top">ROFLMAO!  Too cute!  But I have a feeling that little guy has absolutely no problem at all taking on that big hydrant, little dogs are the toughest, I know, I have two of them, LOL!<br/> <br/>This is a nice shot but it seems to focus more on the hydrant than the dog itself.  Very good humor but not really portrait style.  The light is a bit harsh, maybe a slight adjustment in levels or curves to tone down the light but really make the colors come out?   Or even a conversion to black and white, lots of tones there to work with!  A 6</td>', 'ROFLMAO!  Too cute!  But I have a feeling that little guy has absolutely no problem at all taking on that big hydrant, little dogs are the toughest, I know, I have two of them, LOL! This is a nice shot but it seems to focus more on the hydrant than the dog itself.  Very good humor but not really portrait style.  The light is a bit harsh, maybe a slight adjustment in levels or curves to tone down the light but really make the colors come out?   Or even a conversion to black and white, lots of tones there to work with!  A 6', '2005-04-10 00:58:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(1281585, 161743, 12448, '<td valign="top">OMG, too cute!  I like the duotone with this shot, very well done, not overstated and not too bright.  <br/> <br/>Just a couple of things bother me, first the crop or composition of the shot.  The focus is on the cat''s face so everything right of the door with the cat''s face is not necessary.  If it was solid and providing negative space in that manner it would be one thing but it''s not and it ends up competing for the cat''s face.  And by cropping out the right you also take away my second distraction, the moving string.  A 6</td>', 'OMG, too cute!  I like the duotone with this shot, very well done, not overstated and not too bright.   Just a couple of things bother me, first the crop or composition of the shot.  The focus is on the cat''s face so everything right of the door with the cat''s face is not necessary.  If it was solid and providing negative space in that manner it would be one thing but it''s not and it ends up competing for the cat''s face.  And by cropping out the right you also take away my second distraction, the moving string.  A 6', '2005-04-10 01:00:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(1281586, 162819, 32459, '<td valign="top">This is striking and beautiful...  10</td>', 'This is striking and beautiful...  10', '2005-04-10 01:03:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(1281587, 162941, 12448, '<td valign="top">Aww, Peanut is a doll!  So cute, the sad eyes, the forlorn look!<br/> <br/>Nice capture, very candid and real.  The scene looks like it might have used a flash to get the light, I''m guessing from the darker background.  A tighter crop on the face might really bring out Peanut''s personality more, as it''s set up now he''s competing with the rock on the right and the table or rock he''s laying on.  A 6</td>', 'Aww, Peanut is a doll!  So cute, the sad eyes, the forlorn look! Nice capture, very candid and real.  The scene looks like it might have used a flash to get the light, I''m guessing from the darker background.  A tighter crop on the face might really bring out Peanut''s personality more, as it''s set up now he''s competing with the rock on the right and the table or rock he''s laying on.  A 6', '2005-04-10 01:04:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(1281588, 162700, 12448, '<td valign="top">And just who is he howling or yelling at? :)<br/> <br/>Very cute candid, nice capture, good DOF on the cat to the roses and the lighting is a tad bit harsh, just a tad.  I think you could have cropped more of the roses out, leaving just one or two so the cat really becomes the main focus and isn''t just half the picture.  A 6</td>', 'And just who is he howling or yelling at? :) Very cute candid, nice capture, good DOF on the cat to the roses and the lighting is a tad bit harsh, just a tad.  I think you could have cropped more of the roses out, leaving just one or two so the cat really becomes the main focus and isn''t just half the picture.  A 6', '2005-04-10 01:06:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(1281589, 161837, 32459, '<td valign="top">This is adorable!  8</td>', 'This is adorable!  8', '2005-04-10 01:06:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(1281591, 161869, 12448, '<td valign="top">Jake is beautiful!  So handsome!  I used to have a dog named Jake but he was an English Springer Spaniel!  This is a lovely shot, just a few things that jump out at me, first the lighting, the shadows on the collor area are a tad distracting.  And the fur on the lower right side is starting to blow out, not quite there but close.  Mayber a tighter crop on the bottom just above the buckle would help with that?<br/> <br/>Second the backtround, it almost ends up blending with the dog instead of helping him stand out and the shadow and lines coming in on the right are a tad distracting, again nothing major, just little things.  And did you dodge or burn any of this?  There seems to be a dark halo around Jake in some areas, that is very distracting.  I had this at a 6 but Jake is so wonderful and so loyal (I can tell from his expression) I am raising it to a 7</td>', 'Jake is beautiful!  So handsome!  I used to have a dog named Jake but he was an English Springer Spaniel!  This is a lovely shot, just a few things that jump out at me, first the lighting, the shadows on the collor area are a tad distracting.  And the fur on the lower right side is starting to blow out, not quite there but close.  Mayber a tighter crop on the bottom just above the buckle would help with that? Second the backtround, it almost ends up blending with the dog instead of helping him stand out and the shadow and lines coming in on the right are a tad distracting, again nothing major, just little things.  And did you dodge or burn any of this?  There seems to be a dark halo around Jake in some areas, that is very distracting.  I had this at a 6 but Jake is so wonderful and so loyal (I can tell from his expression) I am raising it to a 7', '2005-04-10 01:09:36.000000', NULL, 1);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(1281593, 162883, 34668, '<td valign="top">It is very difficult to take a photo of a rodent!  My husband tried it - gave the hamster a piece of asparagus, which disappeared into her cheek and off she ran...tried it again with a cracker...same thing and no portrait of the hamster.  Great texture, color, fun photo</td>', 'It is very difficult to take a photo of a rodent!  My husband tried it - gave the hamster a piece of asparagus, which disappeared into her cheek and off she ran...tried it again with a cracker...same thing and no portrait of the hamster.  Great texture, color, fun photo', '2005-04-10 01:09:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(1281596, 161863, 12448, '<td valign="top">I bet Zake loves his frisbee!  He looks like he does!<br/> <br/>Zake is beautiful, the black and white is wonderful, almost makes me wonder what this would look like in gray scale.  I ask because the green/brown/tan grass is competing for attention with Zake and as cute as he is, all attention should be on him!  Maybe a different crop as well?  His back foot is sticking out funny, was it injured or deformed?  If you crop that out, leaving the upper body, head and frisbee I think it might look much better.  A 6</td>', 'I bet Zake loves his frisbee!  He looks like he does! Zake is beautiful, the black and white is wonderful, almost makes me wonder what this would look like in gray scale.  I ask because the green/brown/tan grass is competing for attention with Zake and as cute as he is, all attention should be on him!  Maybe a different crop as well?  His back foot is sticking out funny, was it injured or deformed?  If you crop that out, leaving the upper body, head and frisbee I think it might look much better.  A 6', '2005-04-10 01:12:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(1281599, 162272, 12448, '<td valign="top">OMG!  The expression just makes you LOL!  I bet this little one is a bundle of Joy that keeps you on your toes!<br/> <br/>Very nice shot but the focus is a bit off and the lighting is a bit harsh.  I love the tongue sticking out though, very cute!  A 6</td>', 'OMG!  The expression just makes you LOL!  I bet this little one is a bundle of Joy that keeps you on your toes! Very nice shot but the focus is a bit off and the lighting is a bit harsh.  I love the tongue sticking out though, very cute!  A 6', '2005-04-10 01:14:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(1281600, 163102, 12448, '<td valign="top">The first pass I did on voting I gave Blackie a 6 and upon further and longer inspection I''m trying to figure out what it was that made me do that.  The only thing I can think or see is the edging, I''m not a big fan of this type of border, it takes away from the subject.  And maybe it was the blue color and the shadow on the left side of the neck.  But after taking more time with this shot, there is no way I can leave it at a 6, that would be a crime and I would have to be severly licked to death by Blackie for such an insult.  Am raising to an 8</td>', 'The first pass I did on voting I gave Blackie a 6 and upon further and longer inspection I''m trying to figure out what it was that made me do that.  The only thing I can think or see is the edging, I''m not a big fan of this type of border, it takes away from the subject.  And maybe it was the blue color and the shadow on the left side of the neck.  But after taking more time with this shot, there is no way I can leave it at a 6, that would be a crime and I would have to be severly licked to death by Blackie for such an insult.  Am raising to an 8', '2005-04-10 01:17:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(1281602, 163079, 12448, '<td valign="top">Cool snake, I love snakes, used to hate them but only because my mother did, a snake never did anything to me!<br/> <br/>This is a nice picture but not really a portrait to me.  You are looking all over the place for the subject''s head and the background is very distracting.  Also the lighting is a bit harsh for this shot and the DOF doesn''t really work well, part of the snake fuzzy, part clear.  A 6</td>', 'Cool snake, I love snakes, used to hate them but only because my mother did, a snake never did anything to me! This is a nice picture but not really a portrait to me.  You are looking all over the place for the subject''s head and the background is very distracting.  Also the lighting is a bit harsh for this shot and the DOF doesn''t really work well, part of the snake fuzzy, part clear.  A 6', '2005-04-10 01:19:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(1281606, 162926, 12448, '<td valign="top">Gilbert is a lovely Goose! Fine, nobel features, and very goose like demeanor! ;)<br/> <br/>This is a nice shot, the dof works well with this shot but the background and the goose almost end up blending, both being so gray.  The color on the end of his beak seems off a bit, seems it should be more white but it''s been a long time since I''ve been around geese (my father raised them for years).  I would have also like to possilby see a little more of Gilbert. :)  A 6</td>', 'Gilbert is a lovely Goose! Fine, nobel features, and very goose like demeanor! ;) This is a nice shot, the dof works well with this shot but the background and the goose almost end up blending, both being so gray.  The color on the end of his beak seems off a bit, seems it should be more white but it''s been a long time since I''ve been around geese (my father raised them for years).  I would have also like to possilby see a little more of Gilbert. :)  A 6', '2005-04-10 01:21:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(1281608, 162925, 12448, '<td valign="top">Hahaha, very cute!  Nice candid, humorour shot!  Wish I could see those eyes though@ ;)  The light on his ear is blown out a bit and the DOF of the ear compared to the rest of the shot just doesn''t seem quite right, seems it should be a bit sharper.  A 6</td>', 'Hahaha, very cute!  Nice candid, humorour shot!  Wish I could see those eyes though@ ;)  The light on his ear is blown out a bit and the DOF of the ear compared to the rest of the shot just doesn''t seem quite right, seems it should be a bit sharper.  A 6', '2005-04-10 01:23:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(1281612, 162954, 12448, '<td valign="top">A pet butterfly, riiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiight!<br/> <br/>And I have a pet fly!  But the pesky little bugger wouldn''t sit still for me so I swatted him, LOL!  Just teasing.  You get a point for creativity but sadly, lose a point for not getting a frontal view of said pet so it balances out :)<br/> <br/>This is a lovely shot and any other challenge would have easily gotten an 8 or 9 from me but since it''s pushing the imagination to make it fit the challenge and the flower or whatever that is in the lower right corner is blown out, you will have to settle for a 6, hope that''s okay :)</td>', 'A pet butterfly, riiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiiight! And I have a pet fly!  But the pesky little bugger wouldn''t sit still for me so I swatted him, LOL!  Just teasing.  You get a point for creativity but sadly, lose a point for not getting a frontal view of said pet so it balances out :) This is a lovely shot and any other challenge would have easily gotten an 8 or 9 from me but since it''s pushing the imagination to make it fit the challenge and the flower or whatever that is in the lower right corner is blown out, you will have to settle for a 6, hope that''s okay :)', '2005-04-10 01:25:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(1281613, 162938, 12448, '<td valign="top">Don''t we all dream of summertime, especially as I sit here in my blanket shivering, LOL!<br/> <br/>Very nice shot, the quiet nap like state, the cropping is all done very well.  The lighting is nice, but the background is a bit of a distraction.  I had this at a 6 but am bumping to an 8</td>', 'Don''t we all dream of summertime, especially as I sit here in my blanket shivering, LOL! Very nice shot, the quiet nap like state, the cropping is all done very well.  The lighting is nice, but the background is a bit of a distraction.  I had this at a 6 but am bumping to an 8', '2005-04-10 01:27:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(1281615, 163081, 12448, '<td valign="top">Interesting,I can even see the collar on the human pet as well.<br/> <br/>Nice idea but doesn''t really fit this challenge in the spirit it was intended simply because the viewer is immediately distracted by the lovely young naked lady and the cat get lost in the tonal ranges.  A 6 for clever idea nad not bad shot.</td>', 'Interesting,I can even see the collar on the human pet as well. Nice idea but doesn''t really fit this challenge in the spirit it was intended simply because the viewer is immediately distracted by the lovely young naked lady and the cat get lost in the tonal ranges.  A 6 for clever idea nad not bad shot.', '2005-04-10 01:28:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(1281618, 162906, 12448, '<td valign="top">MINNIE!!! So cute!  I too have a terrier and aren''t they just the most fun!  Mine is a silky and he''s king of the hill around here!  Bet your little one is as well! ;)<br/> <br/>Nice shot, lovely grass, but the back lighting from the sug ends up almost bllowing out the hair on his head and darkens the face too much for me.  A 6</td>', 'MINNIE!!! So cute!  I too have a terrier and aren''t they just the most fun!  Mine is a silky and he''s king of the hill around here!  Bet your little one is as well! ;) Nice shot, lovely grass, but the back lighting from the sug ends up almost bllowing out the hair on his head and darkens the face too much for me.  A 6', '2005-04-10 01:30:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(1281625, 162801, 12448, '<td valign="top">Yes he does!  Love the expression on his face.<br/> <br/>The shot is lacking in light and luster.  Nothing really jumping out at me and making me say, "THIS IS THE ONE!"  It''s a great shot but the dull colors and bit of noise are all a bit distracting and takes too much from the shot.  A 6</td>', 'Yes he does!  Love the expression on his face. The shot is lacking in light and luster.  Nothing really jumping out at me and making me say, "THIS IS THE ONE!"  It''s a great shot but the dull colors and bit of noise are all a bit distracting and takes too much from the shot.  A 6', '2005-04-10 01:32:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(1281629, 163050, 12448, '<td valign="top">The title made me think of the song with the same name, LOL!<br/> <br/>A girl and her best friend, a black dog, a very hard to capture on film or digital black animal.  I know, there are 4 black horses at the barn and 2 black cats in my home and it''s pure luck when I get a good shot of them, LOL!<br/> <br/>I like the idea but it''s not really about friends or pets and their owners, it''s more the pets themselves.  The back lighting is a bit too much, just a slight smudgen too much, causing the dark dog to look even darker with no real defining feature.  Cut the girl out, play with the levels and you got a contender there!  As is a 6</td>', 'The title made me think of the song with the same name, LOL! A girl and her best friend, a black dog, a very hard to capture on film or digital black animal.  I know, there are 4 black horses at the barn and 2 black cats in my home and it''s pure luck when I get a good shot of them, LOL! I like the idea but it''s not really about friends or pets and their owners, it''s more the pets themselves.  The back lighting is a bit too much, just a slight smudgen too much, causing the dark dog to look even darker with no real defining feature.  Cut the girl out, play with the levels and you got a contender there!  As is a 6', '2005-04-10 01:36:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(1281630, 162990, 12448, '<td valign="top">Awwwwwwwwwww, George is beautiful!  How many treats did he get for being so patient?  LOL!<br/> <br/>I love this shot, just one tiny little thing kept it from being perfect and I originally scored it at a 9 but the one thing is so tiny I''m going to overlook it and make this a 10.  Oh, the one thing?  The white stray hair on his ear. :)</td>', 'Awwwwwwwwwww, George is beautiful!  How many treats did he get for being so patient?  LOL! I love this shot, just one tiny little thing kept it from being perfect and I originally scored it at a 9 but the one thing is so tiny I''m going to overlook it and make this a 10.  Oh, the one thing?  The white stray hair on his ear. :)', '2005-04-10 01:36:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(1281634, 162796, 12448, '<td valign="top">Sam is so precious!  I love little dogs like these, so cute and trusting and loyal!<br/> <br/>This is a nice shot, the composition works well with the extra room on the left and the DOF also works well here.  My only complaint is the coloration, his ear seems so orange compared to the rest of him and if that''s the way he is, sorry but it just seems a bit over done for some reason.  A 6 to start but Sam is talking to me saying if he doesn''t at least gat a 7 he''s going to come over and chew up all my wires so I''ll give you an 8 just to be safe!  :)</td>', 'Sam is so precious!  I love little dogs like these, so cute and trusting and loyal! This is a nice shot, the composition works well with the extra room on the left and the DOF also works well here.  My only complaint is the coloration, his ear seems so orange compared to the rest of him and if that''s the way he is, sorry but it just seems a bit over done for some reason.  A 6 to start but Sam is talking to me saying if he doesn''t at least gat a 7 he''s going to come over and chew up all my wires so I''ll give you an 8 just to be safe!  :)', '2005-04-10 01:40:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(1281636, 161746, 12448, '<td valign="top">Yes he is! I love those souful eyes!  So gently yet I just know if I go or do something I''m not supposed to do he''ll let me know! ;)<br/> <br/>Nice shot, I like the angel of coming down but the flash left a big shadow and blew out the white on his chest.  A 6</td>', 'Yes he is! I love those souful eyes!  So gently yet I just know if I go or do something I''m not supposed to do he''ll let me know! ;) Nice shot, I like the angel of coming down but the flash left a big shadow and blew out the white on his chest.  A 6', '2005-04-10 01:41:44.000000', NULL, 1),
