(1282134, 163006, 23412, '<td valign="top">I don''t know about this thing being a pet, but it is a great picture.  Your title is right on the money, too.   Good DOF and crop, IMO.  I could live without the odd little feathers coming out of the bottom left leg area since they are out of focus.  There is also an odd little whisp coming off one of the upper feathers on the left side of the pic.  Might have cloned that out.    Anyway, great subject. After all the cats and dogs, it was nice to see a baby bird.</td>', 'I don''t know about this thing being a pet, but it is a great picture.  Your title is right on the money, too.   Good DOF and crop, IMO.  I could live without the odd little feathers coming out of the bottom left leg area since they are out of focus.  There is also an odd little whisp coming off one of the upper feathers on the left side of the pic.  Might have cloned that out.    Anyway, great subject. After all the cats and dogs, it was nice to see a baby bird.', '2005-04-10 15:42:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(1282136, 161810, 31443, '<td valign="top">What a sweet face!</td>', 'What a sweet face!', '2005-04-10 15:44:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(1282139, 163049, 23412, '<td valign="top">The best of the snake photos IMO.  Your use of the climbing rope adds some color, which was a very good idea.  The snake''s head haning out over the black background is a nice "pose."  The point of focus seems to be more toward the center of the frame, however, and to my eye the head and  tongue seem to be somewhat more soft than I would prefer.  Still a great picture.  Thanks for posting it!</td>', 'The best of the snake photos IMO.  Your use of the climbing rope adds some color, which was a very good idea.  The snake''s head haning out over the black background is a nice "pose."  The point of focus seems to be more toward the center of the frame, however, and to my eye the head and  tongue seem to be somewhat more soft than I would prefer.  Still a great picture.  Thanks for posting it!', '2005-04-10 15:46:05.000000', NULL, 1),
