(1283811, 161985, 31281, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all the comments!  To answer some of them... <br/> <br/>He''s a 9 year old mix breed; half cocker and half black lab.<br/> <br/>As far as the snapshot feel, I would have to agree.  It was taken as I was viewing some other pictures I had taken earlier in the day.  He was cocking his head like that when I talked to him, and he has his signature Alfalfa hair going.   So, I guess it was a snapshot.  But, I had to post it anyways.<br/> <br/>Keep shooting, right?</td>', 'Thanks for all the comments!  To answer some of them...  He''s a 9 year old mix breed; half cocker and half black lab. As far as the snapshot feel, I would have to agree.  It was taken as I was viewing some other pictures I had taken earlier in the day.  He was cocking his head like that when I talked to him, and he has his signature Alfalfa hair going.   So, I guess it was a snapshot.  But, I had to post it anyways. Keep shooting, right?', '2005-04-11 09:47:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(1283814, 161472, 18028, '<td valign="top">well....in the end, not that it matters much,  this shot was not blown out...it was shot using a IR filter and then inverted to get the animal the right color. The background and some of the features are tell tales of the shot not being blown out. I''m not angry about this, a shot should not need to be explained, so I take this "failure" as a learning experience.  <br/> <br/>Thanx for all the comments.</td>', 'well....in the end, not that it matters much,  this shot was not blown out...it was shot using a IR filter and then inverted to get the animal the right color. The background and some of the features are tell tales of the shot not being blown out. I''m not angry about this, a shot should not need to be explained, so I take this "failure" as a learning experience.   Thanx for all the comments.', '2005-04-11 09:49:35.000000', NULL, 0),
