(1284751, 161114, 35229, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by hughletheren:</b></div><hr/><i> This is a really good photograph.  Combined with the humour, it deserved much better! </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Thank you, I thought so too.</td>', 'Originally posted by hughletheren: This is a really good photograph.  Combined with the humour, it deserved much better!  Thank you, I thought so too.', '2005-04-11 20:04:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(1284805, 163085, 23412, '<td valign="top">Thank you to everyone who commented on my picture.  Bayoo is an Oscar.  He will soon be 2 years old, and he lives by himself in a 75 gallon aquarium with an Eheim canister filter and an Acquaclear HOB.  Bayoo loves to eat red Hikari pellets.  The biggest ones they make.  He also likes worms and fake crab meat.  I don''t give him anything else.<br/> <br/>My challenge photo was lit with aquarium lights (I have a standard fluorescent bar that spans the tank and a brighter fluoro setup that is designed more for planted tanks so the light is brighter).  With fish pics, you pretty much have to top light to avoid the room glare on the glass.  I did very little by way of post processing, and according to at least one of the comments, more might have improved my score.  I will have to work on my digital darkroom skills.  CS Elements (2.0) may be the lightweight little brother of the PS family, but it is still pretty complicated for me.  Anyway, thanks again to everyone who commented.<br/></td>', 'Thank you to everyone who commented on my picture.  Bayoo is an Oscar.  He will soon be 2 years old, and he lives by himself in a 75 gallon aquarium with an Eheim canister filter and an Acquaclear HOB.  Bayoo loves to eat red Hikari pellets.  The biggest ones they make.  He also likes worms and fake crab meat.  I don''t give him anything else. My challenge photo was lit with aquarium lights (I have a standard fluorescent bar that spans the tank and a brighter fluoro setup that is designed more for planted tanks so the light is brighter).  With fish pics, you pretty much have to top light to avoid the room glare on the glass.  I did very little by way of post processing, and according to at least one of the comments, more might have improved my score.  I will have to work on my digital darkroom skills.  CS Elements (2.0) may be the lightweight little brother of the PS family, but it is still pretty complicated for me.  Anyway, thanks again to everyone who commented.', '2005-04-11 20:31:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(1284899, 162922, 12448, '<td valign="top">I didn''t get a chance to comment on this one before the challenge ended.  I had given this shot an 8.  The lighting and distracting pillows in the background were what lost you points with me.  This is a lovely overall shot, the composition, the setting (just cover the pillows) and the lighting seems just a bit harsh.  It should have done much better than it did.</td>', 'I didn''t get a chance to comment on this one before the challenge ended.  I had given this shot an 8.  The lighting and distracting pillows in the background were what lost you points with me.  This is a lovely overall shot, the composition, the setting (just cover the pillows) and the lighting seems just a bit harsh.  It should have done much better than it did.', '2005-04-11 21:45:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(1284928, 162614, 12448, '<td valign="top">I didn''t get to this one during the challenge.  I gave this one a 7, I have a very soft spot for calicos so that earned you an extra point right there! :)<br/> <br/>This is a lovely, relaxing shot and well composed.  The only thing that bothered me was the dark edges.  I''m not a big fan of burning the edges to darkly for a shot.  If you just used a vinette filter then , well, still, not my personal taste.  But still a lovely kitty, give Trouble some scritches for me, kay?</td>', 'I didn''t get to this one during the challenge.  I gave this one a 7, I have a very soft spot for calicos so that earned you an extra point right there! :) This is a lovely, relaxing shot and well composed.  The only thing that bothered me was the dark edges.  I''m not a big fan of burning the edges to darkly for a shot.  If you just used a vinette filter then , well, still, not my personal taste.  But still a lovely kitty, give Trouble some scritches for me, kay?', '2005-04-11 22:05:50.000000', NULL, 0),
