(1285062, 162083, 12448, '<td valign="top">I didn''t get a chance to get to this one during the challenge but I will go ahead and comment now.  I gave this a 7 and here is the reasoning.  I love the dog.  I love the expression and I even love the slightly off center.  What bugs me though the most is the lighting.  There is some nice bright light in the back (too bright for what you want) and while it could work for back lighting, it''s too far back and ends up being distracting instead.  I''m not a fan of dodging and burning but this is one situation where just a slight amount, burn the back just a bit and dodge the dog just a touch would really bring the balance of light back.  Hope this helps!</td>', 'I didn''t get a chance to get to this one during the challenge but I will go ahead and comment now.  I gave this a 7 and here is the reasoning.  I love the dog.  I love the expression and I even love the slightly off center.  What bugs me though the most is the lighting.  There is some nice bright light in the back (too bright for what you want) and while it could work for back lighting, it''s too far back and ends up being distracting instead.  I''m not a fan of dodging and burning but this is one situation where just a slight amount, burn the back just a bit and dodge the dog just a touch would really bring the balance of light back.  Hope this helps!', '2005-04-11 23:27:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(1285065, 162918, 32997, '<td valign="top">Great sense of drama you have captured here. The next moment is clear in her eyes, the grass gives wonderful context.  The tight crop works wonderfully in bringing her eyes to the forefront, yet also flattens her face a bit, making it look slightly disorted-it is hard to tell that the upper corners go back, they seem to fill out to the sides. Perhaps a slighly wider crop would have given necessary perspective. Really crisp shot, focus and depth excellent. I had given this shot a 6, and if not for the flattening of the head would have scored higher.</td>', 'Great sense of drama you have captured here. The next moment is clear in her eyes, the grass gives wonderful context.  The tight crop works wonderfully in bringing her eyes to the forefront, yet also flattens her face a bit, making it look slightly disorted-it is hard to tell that the upper corners go back, they seem to fill out to the sides. Perhaps a slighly wider crop would have given necessary perspective. Really crisp shot, focus and depth excellent. I had given this shot a 6, and if not for the flattening of the head would have scored higher.', '2005-04-11 23:33:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(1285067, 163019, 12448, '<td valign="top">Hi!  I didn''t get a chance to comment during the challenge so here goes.  I gave this shot a 7.  I like the conversion to black and white and I like the overall feel of the shot, the textures, the relaxed mode it put me in. You must have wore that little guy out!  <br/> <br/>I never noticed the one eye peeking out, it''s almost hidden and I think that was part of why I started with a 7 on this, had I been able to get back to it I would have probably bumped to an 8.  The overall shot lacks the contrast needed to really make it stand out but an excellent shot still the same. :)</td>', 'Hi!  I didn''t get a chance to comment during the challenge so here goes.  I gave this shot a 7.  I like the conversion to black and white and I like the overall feel of the shot, the textures, the relaxed mode it put me in. You must have wore that little guy out!   I never noticed the one eye peeking out, it''s almost hidden and I think that was part of why I started with a 7 on this, had I been able to get back to it I would have probably bumped to an 8.  The overall shot lacks the contrast needed to really make it stand out but an excellent shot still the same. :)', '2005-04-11 23:35:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(1285080, 162940, 32997, '<td valign="top">Great story, and really adorable look on his face. The angle really works here-I just wish you could have got him to look toward the camera. Lighting is excellent.</td>', 'Great story, and really adorable look on his face. The angle really works here-I just wish you could have got him to look toward the camera. Lighting is excellent.', '2005-04-11 23:47:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(1285087, 161837, 255, '<td valign="top"><i>"i wish you wouldnt keep appearing and vanishing so suddenly, you make one quite giddy." <br/> <br/>"all right", said the cat, and this time it vanished quite slowly, beginning with the end of the tail, and ending with the grin, which remained some time after the rest of it had gone. <br/> <br/></i> <br/>awesome, this is a real-deal cheshire cat if i have have seen one. :)</td>', '"i wish you wouldnt keep appearing and vanishing so suddenly, you make one quite giddy."  "all right", said the cat, and this time it vanished quite slowly, beginning with the end of the tail, and ending with the grin, which remained some time after the rest of it had gone.   awesome, this is a real-deal cheshire cat if i have have seen one. :)', '2005-04-11 23:51:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(1285100, 163018, 255, '<td valign="top">lovely composition and perfect lighting...but the icing is the very wry, human expression on knickers. i get the feeling that if she could be raising one brow at you, she would be. :)</td>', 'lovely composition and perfect lighting...but the icing is the very wry, human expression on knickers. i get the feeling that if she could be raising one brow at you, she would be. :)', '2005-04-11 23:59:13.000000', NULL, 0),
