(2526074, 162863, 36076, '<td valign="top">this photo really made me smile. simply precious! i''m not usually a fan of small dogs, but this shot really makes me want one! fantastic focus. i love the way his eyes come to life and we can see even the tiniest details of his face. the colors are amazing as well. so crisp and bright. they really add to the shot. the black bg makes for an excellent backdrop and makes your little dogs face pop right out of the composition and i have to say the pink really does flatter him (not to mention i''m in love with the o so soft texture of the feathers).</td>', 'this photo really made me smile. simply precious! i''m not usually a fan of small dogs, but this shot really makes me want one! fantastic focus. i love the way his eyes come to life and we can see even the tiniest details of his face. the colors are amazing as well. so crisp and bright. they really add to the shot. the black bg makes for an excellent backdrop and makes your little dogs face pop right out of the composition and i have to say the pink really does flatter him (not to mention i''m in love with the o so soft texture of the feathers).', '2006-06-18 12:28:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(2604325, 163019, 52130, '<td valign="top">Cute Shot. Yeah, I noticed the similarities between my dog, Buddy, and Ben. I got buddy from my best friend''s house back in 2000 when her dogs, Ginger and Scamp had 7 puppies. Scamp (whom I believe to be one of the grungiest-looking dogs ever) is half Jack Russel/Wirehaired Terrier, and Ginger is a purebred half miniature, half toy poodle(I have her sister, Rosie). So, what do you get when you put them together? A Terri-dac-dle. Yup, Terrier Dacshund, poodle.<br/> <br/>While I don''t think that Ben is related to Buddy, I do think that he is a similar mix. The only reason I don''t think so, is b/c I knew all of the puppies and you live in Texas. There were 4 black and tan ones, 1 brown one, 1 redhead (buddy), and 1 white, who was a girl. I''m so frustrated that I can''t find the pic of them when they were pups! Darn. Here are some other ones: <br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=361164" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/52130/thumb/361164.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/52130/thumb/361164.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/52130/thumb/361164.jpg"/></a><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=361165" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/52130/thumb/361165.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/52130/thumb/361165.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/52130/thumb/361165.jpg"/></a><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=361174" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/52130/thumb/361174.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/52130/thumb/361174.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/52130/thumb/361174.jpg"/></a><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=361166" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/52130/thumb/361166.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/52130/thumb/361166.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/52130/thumb/361166.jpg"/></a><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-07-09 21:09:33.</i></td>', 'Cute Shot. Yeah, I noticed the similarities between my dog, Buddy, and Ben. I got buddy from my best friend''s house back in 2000 when her dogs, Ginger and Scamp had 7 puppies. Scamp (whom I believe to be one of the grungiest-looking dogs ever) is half Jack Russel/Wirehaired Terrier, and Ginger is a purebred half miniature, half toy poodle(I have her sister, Rosie). So, what do you get when you put them together? A Terri-dac-dle. Yup, Terrier Dacshund, poodle. While I don''t think that Ben is related to Buddy, I do think that he is a similar mix. The only reason I don''t think so, is b/c I knew all of the puppies and you live in Texas. There were 4 black and tan ones, 1 brown one, 1 redhead (buddy), and 1 white, who was a girl. I''m so frustrated that I can''t find the pic of them when they were pups! Darn. Here are some other ones:  ', '2006-07-09 22:07:35.000000', '2006-07-09 22:09:33.000000', 0),
